{title: 495 - Near to the Heart of God}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #495 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Db}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 495}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Db]There is a place ofquiet [Ab7]rest,
[Ab7]Near to the heart of [Db]God;
[Db]A place where sin can [Ab7/Eb]not mo lest,
[Ab7]Near to the [Db/Ab]heart [Ab]of [Db]God.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Db]O [Gb]Jesus, blest Redeemer,
[Ab]sent from the [Ab7]heart of [Db]God,
[Db]hold [Gb]us who wait before [Db]thee
[Ab7]near to the heart of [Db]God.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Db]There is a place of [Ab7/Eb]comfort sweet,
[Ab7]near to the heart of [Db]God;
[Db]a place where we our [Ab7/Eb]Savior meet,
[Ab7]near to the [Db/Ab]heart [Ab]of [Db]God.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Db]There is place a place of [Ab7/Eb]full release,
[Ab7]near to the heart of [Db]God;
[Db]a place where all is [Ab7/Eb]joy and peace,
[Ab7]near to the [Db/Ab]heart [Ab]of [Db]God.
{end_of_verse}
